    "shape:agent_label": {
      "id": "shape:agent_label",
      "typeName": "shape",
      "meta": {},
      "parentId": "page:page",
      "index": "b8",
      "x": 520,
      "y": 1200,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "props": {
        "color": "black",
        "text": "INTELLIGENCE LAYER (L3) — Agent vs Deterministic mapping\n\nAgent (or candidate):\n  C2  Scenario Understanding (intent parsing)\n  C5  Scenario Generation (decision-making; XML output stays deterministic)\n  C6  Scenario Exploration (which scenario next)\n  C10 Scenario Repair (error → fix → regenerate)\n  C9  Scenario Analysis (interpretation of outcomes)\n\nDeterministic:\n  C3  Knowledge / RAG retrieval\n  C4  IR data model\n  C7  Validation (XSD, semantic, physical, runtime)\n  C8  esmini execution engine\n  C11 Scenario Management (storage)",
        "font": "mono",
        "size": "s",
        "textAlign": "left",
        "verticalAlign": "top",
        "w": 480,
        "h": 220
      }
    },

    "shape:flow_label": {
      "id": "shape:flow_label",
      "typeName": "shape",
      "meta": {},
      "parentId": "page:page",
      "index": "b9",
      "x": 1020,
      "y": 1200,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "props": {
        "color": "black",
        "text": "DATA FLOW — One User Request\n\n1.  User request enters C1 (Input)\n2.  C2 (Understanding) parses intent → structured scenario IR\n3.  C2 queries C3 (Knowledge) for OpenSCENARIO / OpenDRIVE / esmini schemas & rules\n4.  C2 + C3 produce C4 (IR) — internal structured scenario description\n5.  C4 feeds C5 (Generation) and C6 (Exploration)\n6.  C5 constructs scenario; C6 varies parameters (sweep, Monte Carlo, edge cases)\n7.  C4 + C5 compile → .xosc / .xodr files (deterministic output)\n8.  C7 (Validation) checks: XML/XSD → semantic → physical plausibility → runtime dry-run\n9.  If FAIL → C10 (Repair) classifies error, modifies IR, loops back to C5\n   If PASS → C8 (esmini Simulation) loads & executes the scenario\n10. C8 runs scenario: storyboard, triggers, entity & road simulation, external controllers\n11. C8 emits OSI ground truth, entity states, logs\n12. C9 (Observation) collects states; C9 (Evaluation) computes TTC, collision, lane departure, safety score\n13. C9 results + C10 (Analysis) rank scenarios, find critical/near-miss cases\n14. C10 (Feedback) → C6 (Exploration) to generate next batch or mutate interesting scenarios\n15. C11 (Management) stores everything: IR, .xosc/.xodr, validation results, run data, metrics, logs, versions\n\n(Closed-loop: output of C9/C10 feeds back into C6/C10 for iterative exploration)",
        "font": "mono",
        "size": "s",
        "textAlign": "left",
        "verticalAlign": "top",
        "w": 460,
        "h": 400
      }
    },

